 R←TestDrivers;m;b;unchanged;new;retired;missing;differ;present
⍝ Stage 3: SkyAt and Entry replace ENTRY, CALCULATEPLANETS and
⍝ CALCULATESTARS; the input prompts are copied unchanged.
⍝ Entry prompts for date, time, latitude and longitude and returns
⍝ STATEDDAYNO STATEDTIME LAT LONG, the right argument of SkyAt.
 m←## ⋄ b←##.Data ⋄ R←1
 unchanged←'GETDATE' 'GETTIME' 'GETLAT' 'GETLONG'
 new←'SkyAt' 'Entry'
 retired←'ENTRY' 'CALCULATEPLANETS' 'CALCULATESTARS'

 missing←(unchanged,new)/⍨3≠⌊m.⎕NC unchanged,new
 :If 0≠≢missing
     ⎕←'FAIL: TestDrivers: missing: ',⍕missing ⋄ R←0
 :EndIf
 differ←unchanged/⍨~{(m.⎕NR ⍵)≡b.⎕NR ⍵}¨unchanged
 :If 0≠≢differ
     ⎕←'FAIL: TestDrivers: source differs from book: ',⍕differ ⋄ R←0
 :EndIf
 present←retired/⍨0≠m.⎕NC retired
 :If 0≠≢present
     ⎕←'FAIL: TestDrivers: retired names present: ',⍕present ⋄ R←0
 :EndIf
 :If 1 0 0≢3↑⊃m.⎕AT'Entry'
     ⎕←'FAIL: TestDrivers: Entry must be niladic with a result' ⋄ R←0
 :EndIf
 :If R
     ⎕←'PASS: TestDrivers'
 :EndIf
